        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cbca5ce0-bc81-5485-a4e9-9f19f428752f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Achel Abbey, Orval Abbey, Cistercians of Strict Observance\n- Places: Achel, Campine, Limburg, Flanders, Belgium, Netherlands, Austria, Italy, United States\n- Products: Trappist beer, Authentic Trappist Product, Orval cheese\n- Topics: Spiritual life, Trappist breweries\n\nFacts:\n- Achel Abbey, also called Saint Benedictus-Abbey or Achelse Kluis, belongs to the Cistercians of Strict Observance.\n- Achel Abbey is located in Achel in the Campine region of Limburg in Flanders, Belgium.\n- Achel Abbey is known for its spiritual life and for its brewery, which is one of the few Trappist beer breweries in the world.\n- Eleven monasteries currently brew beer and sell it as Authentic Trappist Product.\n- The eleven monasteries are located as six in Belgium, two in the Netherlands, and one each in Austria, Italy, and the United States.\n- Orval Abbey is known for its history and spiritual life and for producing the Trappist beer Orval and a specific cheese.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
